WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.136
After approval, sign in with your own username or email and password.

5
00:00:05.136 --> 00:00:10.953
This recording uses fictional records, simulated email, location and a test camera.

9
00:00:10.953 --> 00:00:12.635
No live work is created.

13
00:00:13.435 --> 00:00:20.159
People and access supports multiple NPI administrators and multiple administrators per subcontractor.

17
00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:22.423
Choose the role and invited email.

21
00:00:22.423 --> 00:00:25.818
Select a company for a subcontractor administrator.

25
00:00:25.818 --> 00:00:28.615
Each person creates their own credentials.

29
00:00:29.415 --> 00:00:34.122
Pending approvals shows registrations separately from active people.

33
00:00:34.122 --> 00:00:37.653
Inspect the email and role, then approve or reject.

37
00:00:37.653 --> 00:00:42.846
A new NPI administrator must be approved by the inviting NPI administrator.

41
00:00:42.846 --> 00:00:45.546
Access changes are recorded in history.

45
00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:50.953
Set up the main contract, authorised sites and subcontractor access once.

49
00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:53.415
Invite the subcontractor administrator.

53
00:00:53.415 --> 00:00:58.275
Their approved workers can then start work without waiting for an assignment.

57
00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:03.390
Settings holds each contract’s line items and sub-line items.

61
00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:08.130
Codes stay in management records; workers see simple service names.

65
00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.506
New snow services stay in draft until bands cover zero upwards without gaps.

69
00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:16.548
The Below 2 inches band is created for you.

73
00:01:16.548 --> 00:01:20.580
Activate the parent after completing the remaining bands.

77
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.207
No prices are included.

81
00:01:23.007 --> 00:01:27.867
Use the overview and NPI verification queue to review submitted work.

85
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:29.698
The company reviews first.

89
00:01:29.698 --> 00:01:36.178
Current activity, open issues and exceptions are visible without creating daily assignments.

93
00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:42.878
Inspect the same crew, services, quantities and snow evidence that the company reviewed.

97
00:01:42.878 --> 00:01:46.432
Recorded, claimed and accepted hours remain separate.

101
00:01:46.432 --> 00:01:50.254
Multiple service lines do not multiply worker attendance.

105
00:01:51.054 --> 00:01:53.247
Acknowledge the below-two-inch flag.

109
00:01:53.247 --> 00:01:57.329
Accept the exact claimed hours or enter a correction with a reason.

113
00:01:57.329 --> 00:01:59.826
Return incomplete records to the company.

117
00:01:59.826 --> 00:02:03.725
Original photos, attendance and the review history are retained.

121
00:02:04.525 --> 00:02:10.614
Generate a report for the selected period, company, site, worker, service and status.

125
00:02:10.614 --> 00:02:15.485
CSV and Excel contain every matching row, beyond the on-screen page.

129
00:02:15.485 --> 00:02:21.574
Recorded, claimed and approved hours remain separate and are counted once per worker.

133
00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:24.980
Download a PDF summary for sharing.

137
00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.587
Full detail stays in CSV and Excel.

141
00:02:27.587 --> 00:02:31.608
Evidence reports reference authenticated work records.

145
00:02:31.608 --> 00:02:35.853
Select up to twenty originals for a private evidence ZIP.

149
00:02:35.853 --> 00:02:40.247
Exported report links never expose permanent public photos.

153
00:02:41.047 --> 00:02:43.700
The management workbook keeps seven tabs.

157
00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.158
Supabase remains the primary database.

161
00:02:46.158 --> 00:02:52.757
Permitted site and unstarted planning edits return for NPI review; hours and approvals stay protected.

165
00:02:52.757 --> 00:02:55.474
Settings shows the latest successful sync.

169
00:02:55.474 --> 00:03:00.650
Hide recognised legacy tabs only after a successful refresh; no data is deleted.

173
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:06.647
Configure notification recipients and optional daily summaries in Settings.

177
00:03:06.647 --> 00:03:12.191
A verified email sender is required for new registrations and password recovery.

181
00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:14.201
Existing users remain active.

185
00:03:14.201 --> 00:03:20.368
Apply migration eight, update the function and workbook script, then deploy the frontend.

189
00:03:20.368 --> 00:03:24.873
Test real email and GPS before using the upgrade for live shifts.
